<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<launch>
  <!--
    CARLA Vehicle Interface Launch File

    This is a minimal vehicle interface launch file for CARLA simulation.

    Design Decision:
    ================
    For CARLA simulation, the bridge subscribes directly to /control/command/control_cmd
    and converts ControlCommand to CARLA VehicleControl internally. This eliminates the
    need for the raw_vehicle_cmd_converter node since:

    1. CARLA has ideal actuators - no pedal mapping or calibration needed
    2. Simple linear conversion: acceleration -> throttle/brake, steering_angle -> steer
    3. Reduces pipeline complexity for simulation use case
    4. Bridge implements CARLA-specific vehicle control mapping

    Data Flow:
    ==========
    Autoware Control → /control/command/control_cmd → Bridge → CARLA VehicleControl

    If actuation-level control is needed in the future (for hardware-in-the-loop testing
    or comparison with real vehicles), the raw_vehicle_cmd_converter node can be added
    back here to convert ControlCommand to ActuationCommand.

    Alternative Configuration (not currently used):
    ===============================================
    <arg name="config_file" default="$(find-pkg-share carla_vehicle_launch)/config/raw_vehicle_cmd_converter/raw_vehicle_cmd_converter.param.yaml"/>

    <node pkg="autoware_raw_vehicle_cmd_converter" exec="autoware_raw_vehicle_cmd_converter_node" name="raw_vehicle_cmd_converter">
      <param from="$(var config_file)" allow_substs="true"/>
      <remap from="~/input/control_cmd" to="/control/command/control_cmd"/>
      <remap from="~/output/actuation_cmd" to="/control/command/actuation_cmd"/>
    </node>
  -->
</launch>
